    {
      "body": "Ran the repository pre-commit hooks locally with the same `.pre-commit-config.yaml`; all hooks now pass after applying the import-order fix in 719a820. The updated commit is pushed to the PR branch. I also requested a rerun of the previously egress-limited Actions run.",
      "created_at": "2026-10-31T04:39:08Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/THUDM/slime/pull/2510#issuecomment-6539107221",
      "id": 6539107221,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-31T04:39:08Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "lll-hhh"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "I ran main and this branch through grade_answer_verl on the cases from #2509. The reported ones are all fixed, and so are the same magnitudes written other ways: \"9007199254740993.0\", \"9.007199254740993e15\", and \"1e20\" against 100000000000000000001 all grade True on main and correctly grade False here.\n\nControls behave the same on both -- exact matches, the big \\frac pair, and comma-grouped digits.\nthere's one behavior change i noticed -- the old _normalize path had a 1e-7 integer tolerance, so answers within that band of an integer reference passed -- 41.99999999 and 42.00000001 against 42 both grade True on main and False on this branch.",
      "created_at": "2026-10-31T21:17:06Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/THUDM/slime/pull/2510#issuecomment-6549250030",
      "id": 6549250030,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-31T21:17:06Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "saloni-garg"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "Thanks for running these cases and pointing out the compatibility regression. I restored the legacy 1e-7 integer tolerance while keeping Decimal-based parsing to preserve large-integer precision. I added regression tests for both reported values and values outside the tolerance; the focused math reward suite passes (36 tests). The fix is pushed in 69e69fd.",
      "created_at": "2026-11-01T04:43:42Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/THUDM/slime/pull/2510#issuecomment-6553532082",
      "id": 6553532082,
      "updated_at": "2026-11-01T04:43:42Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "lll-hhh"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "<!-- ci-followup-20261101 -->\nFollowing up on CI for head `69e69fd`: the math reward jobs (`test_rm_math.py` and `test_rm_math_dapo.py`) and pre-commit passed. Across the head's 113 checks, 103 succeeded, 9 were skipped and one failed.\n\nThe [failed CP-whitening job](https://github.com/THUDM/slime/actions/runs/41274181563/job/124752884441) reports `test_whitened_advantages_are_cp_invariant[1-4]` exiting with `torch.multiprocessing.spawn.ProcessExitedException: process 0 terminated with signal SIGABRT`; the other five cases in that job passed. This PR changes only `slime/rollout/rm_hub/math_utils.py` and `tests/test_rm_math.py`. The [same CP-whitening job on base 540ea919](https://github.com/THUDM/slime/actions/runs/40445960764/job/121997185657) passed. This suggests a possible intermittent distributed-process failure, but I have not established its cause.\n\nI attempted to rerun just the failed job, but GitHub returned 403 for insufficient repository permissions. Could a maintainer rerun that job on the current head? If it reproduces, the new log would help distinguish a persistent failure from a transient one.\n",
      "created_at": "2026-11-01T13:22:36Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/THUDM/slime/pull/2510#issuecomment-6558534959",
      "id": 6558534959,
      "updated_at": "2026-11-01T13:22:36Z",
